#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "654b3963-72be-5d2d-ab21-468291cae36b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289128} {:answer/id #uuid "9c08afd9-7502-5e45-bcae-5d34da2f52b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289129} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fb474c-7e53-5437-9a65-388ead62564c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289130} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b781ec-938b-5f02-8e23-aac6bda548c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289131} {:answer/id #uuid "20e24aae-7294-5f43-b360-89d0d52fcba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20e24aae-7294-5f43-b360-89d0d52fcba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289132} :answer-field/id #uuid "097e307a-baf0-562a-a260-70b760dce7bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e39f59c6-1dff-56e6-932b-2ba7bba5a751" :question/math-academy-id "q-114297" :question/problem "$\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289140 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f55817f1-d0c7-5040-b35e-ec4ee3f947ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289142} {:answer/id #uuid "9282af3b-81a0-582a-84c3-c48741017a33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289143} {:answer/id #uuid "644b3aaf-cefd-5234-8335-739a32ab175c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289144} {:answer/id #uuid "6241a189-3434-5fa7-bd6a-1f84f8396f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289145} {:answer/id #uuid "fb574e6c-2f2a-5f5c-8b49-3b144168df1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9282af3b-81a0-582a-84c3-c48741017a33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289143} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2ca7314-1853-5a2e-a8a4-327cd176b8ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9ee642b-9c85-56dd-a07d-2fe51c8fec98" :question/math-academy-id "q-114314" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={csc}^{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ where $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
